---
title: "Home"
description: "Design a clearer home using civica.uk styles, components and patterns."
---
<section class="c-hero"><div class="c-container c-hero__inner"><div><h1>Design your home using civica.uk styles, components and patterns</h1><p>Make Home Assistant clear, consistent and easier to use. Start with established public service design, adapted for the devices, information and everyday tasks in your home.</p><a class="c-start-button" href="<%= docs_path('/get-started/index.html') %>">Get started <span aria-hidden="true">❯</span></a></div><img src="<%= docs_path('/images/design-system-hero.svg') %>" alt="" width="420" height="350"></div></section>
<section class="c-container c-project-intro" aria-labelledby="project-purpose"><h2 id="project-purpose">Why I created civica.uk</h2><p>I created civica.uk to make everyday Home Assistant controls clearer for the whole household, including older relatives, neurodivergent people and guests. This independent project adapts the GOV.UK Design System’s research and reusable patterns into predictable layouts, readable text and clear actions. It is not affiliated with GOV.UK or the UK government.</p><p><a href="<%= docs_path('/get-started/about.html') %>">Read about the project and why I created it</a></p></section>
<section class="c-whats-new"><div class="c-container"><h2>What’s new</h2><div class="c-home-columns"><div><h3>12 November 2026: Home Assistant coverage and writing guidance</h3><p>Explore <a href="<%= docs_path('/home-assistant/index.html') %>">38 Home Assistant specifications</a> for device controls and household tasks. The <a href="<%= docs_path('/content/index.html') %>">Writing guide</a> now has its own section, with plain English guidance and a dated Home Assistant terminology reference.</p><p><a href="<%= docs_path('/community/home-assistant-coverage-audit.html') %>">Read the coverage and verification record</a></p></div><div><h3>Follow the project</h3><p>Read release notes and follow changes in the public repository.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/nathcymru/HA-Theme-gov.uk/releases">View releases on GitHub</a></p></div></div></div></section>
<section class="c-container c-home-categories" aria-label="Explore the design system">
<article><img src="<%= docs_path('/images/category-styles.svg') %>" alt="" width="320" height="140"><h2><a href="<%= docs_path('/styles/index.html') %>">Styles</a></h2><p>Use colour, typography, spacing and imagery to create a recognisable, accessible interface.</p><ul><li><a href="<%= docs_path('/styles/colour.html') %>">Colour and ten brand palettes</a></li><li><a href="<%= docs_path('/styles/chart-colour.html') %>">Chart colours</a></li><li><a href="<%= docs_path('/styles/typography.html') %>">Typography</a></li></ul></article>
<article><img src="<%= docs_path('/images/category-components.svg') %>" alt="" width="320" height="140"><h2><a href="<%= docs_path('/components/index.html') %>">Components</a></h2><p>Build with reusable elements, from buttons and forms to device cards and charts.</p><ul><li><a href="<%= docs_path('/components/buttons.html') %>">Buttons</a></li><li><a href="<%= docs_path('/components/cards.html') %>">Cards</a></li><li><a href="<%= docs_path('/components/example.html') %>">Example component</a></li></ul></article>
<article><img src="<%= docs_path('/images/category-patterns.svg') %>" alt="" width="320" height="140"><h2><a href="<%= docs_path('/patterns/index.html') %>">Patterns</a></h2><p>Combine components to help people complete common tasks and understand their home.</p><ul><li><a href="<%= docs_path('/patterns/home.html') %>">Home and rooms</a></li><li><a href="<%= docs_path('/patterns/question-pages.html') %>">Question pages and dialogs</a></li><li><a href="<%= docs_path('/patterns/british-sign-language.html') %>">British Sign Language</a></li></ul></article>
</section>
<section class="c-home-band"><div class="c-container c-home-columns"><div><h2>Writing guide</h2><p>Use plain English to explain what the home is doing, what someone can change and what happens next. Find guidance for labels, instructions, alerts and Home Assistant terminology.</p><a href="<%= docs_path('/content/index.html') %>">Write for a connected home</a></div><div><h2>Know what is implemented</h2><p>A reference example describes a design. A theme changes appearance. The optional companion adds specific interactions. Each has a different scope.</p><a href="<%= docs_path('/get-started/compatibility.html') %>">Check compatibility and limits</a></div></div></section>
<section class="c-container c-home-columns c-home-support"><div><h2>Design for everyone</h2><p>Build around readable content, keyboard access, clear focus, useful labels and alternatives to visual information.</p><a href="<%= docs_path('/accessibility/index.html') %>">Accessibility principles and checks</a></div><div><h2>Help improve the system</h2><p>Share evidence from real household tasks. Document differences, test examples and keep guidance connected to the implementation.</p><a href="<%= docs_path('/community/index.html') %>">Contribute to civica.uk</a></div></section>
